.DS_Store
/.build
/.index-build
/Examples/.build

# Generated test app packages and their build trees. One per backend: the
# default build and a -gtk4 build cannot share a tree, because SwiftPM's
# incremental state records module dependencies and they contradict each other.
/testapp/.compile-work
/testapp/.compile-work-*

# Reusable iOS Simulator bundle assembled by testapp/test_ios.zsh. The
# template is tracked; the copied debugTarget executable and its signature are
# local build output.
/testapp/.bundledApp/
/testapp/.androidApk/
/testapp/.macApp/
/testapp/.android-sdk/

# Held while one Pn is under test, so two tests cannot produce screenshots of
# each other, plus .ui-lock-denied: the last thing the desktop did with our
# synthesised input. Runtime state, never committed. See testapp/ui-lock.zsh.
/testapp/.ui-lock
/testapp/.ui-lock-denied

# The tree SCUI_HOST_BACKENDS_ONLY=1 swift test builds into, for the same reason
# as the two above: it declares a different set of targets, so it cannot share
# /.build. See the note beside the flag in Package.swift.
/.build-hosttest
/Packages
/*.xcodeproj
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
.swiftpm/xcode/package.xcworkspace/contents.xcworkspacedata
/.vscode
*.pyc
.swiftpm
vcpkg_installed/
*.trace
notes.json
/Tools
.docc-build/
.idea

# A Pn writes this into whatever directory it is launched from. Widened from
# p6-debug-events.log when a P19 run produced p19-debug-events.log -- the name
# is built from the app, so the pattern has to be too.
p*-debug-events.log

# The same shape, but these names carry no app, so p*- cannot cover them: one is
# written by the replay runner and one by SplitView, both from
# currentDirectoryPath. run.zsh launches by absolute path and never cd's, so
# they land in the repo root rather than testapp/output/ -- which is where the
# docs used to say to look for them.
#
# Untracked rather than committed because they are the output of a run, not a
# record of one. A finding worth keeping goes in bugs/ or a note beside the
# action file, quoted; the file itself is regenerated by the next run and would
# only ever conflict.
#
# 同一種東西，但這兩個名稱不含 app，因此 p*- 涵蓋不到：一個由重放 runner 寫出，一個由
# SplitView 寫出，兩者都取自 currentDirectoryPath。run.zsh 以絕對路徑啟動且從不 cd，所以它們
# 落在 repo 根目錄，而非文件過去所說的 testapp/output/。
#
# 不納入版控而是忽略，因為它們是一次執行的產物，不是那次執行的紀錄。值得保留的發現應寫進
# bugs/ 或動作檔旁的註解並直接引用；檔案本身會被下一次執行覆寫，留著只會造成衝突。
actionfile-replay.log
splitview-debug.log
decoration-debug.log
